Since this year will be our 10th Anniversary, we're starting work on it
a bit earlier than usual and we need some player feedback for some of
the preparations.

a)	The new Challenge patch is written and being tested, though the parts
of the Challenge that are outside NetHack itself still need some work.
We should be ready to release the game server kit before the end of
August, so we can get some testing on a variety of servers.  Please
contact us early this year if you want to run a game server, since this
is the biggest Challenge we've done so far and it needs as much testing
as we can give it.

b)	We will be producing some Tournament swag again, after not having
done so since our first year.  Current plans are:

	the basic Dungeons of Doom edition of FridgeHack, the new roguelike you
can play on your refrigerator door

	an illustrated version of Roger Barnett's "Twas the Night Before DevNull"

	a sticker (design suggestions welcome)

	a t-shirt (design suggestions welcome)

We need some idea of how many to have made, so please let us know what
you're interested in (we expect the whole set to be around $30).

c)	If there's enough interest, we will do an opening night party
somewhere in the San Francisco Bay area so please let us know if you're
interested in that as well.

d)	We've been told by a few folks that /dev/null/nethack is the
longest-running online gaming tournament on the Net.  At 10 years, it's
certainly older than any other tournaments we were able to find in a few
minutes on Google, including two others which both claimed to be the
oldest themselves (at 4 and 6 years respectively).  Before we use this
assertion on any of the swag, though, can any of you shed some light on
whether this is actually true?

You can contact us at tournament@nethack.devnull.net.

Thank you all for making the Tournament such fun to put on; we'll see
you in October!

-robin

